{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If he sell his daughter as a maidservant.</b> She is a minor, who is under the father's authority, like a daughter whose vow he can annul. And the phrase 'to a foreign people' is joined with this verse, for it speaks about the father [selling] to a foreign people."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:40.425018115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}